  ],
  "aiContextParagraph": "Various regions across Indonesia are currently grappling with widespread flooding and landslides following heavy seasonal rains. According to national disaster management agencies and local authorities, thousands of families have been affected across Sumatra, Kalimantan, and parts of Java. Significant impacts include the inundation of residential areas, the suspension of school activities in Palembang, and traffic congestion along major routes such as the Pantura road in Demak. In Aceh, authorities are providing emergency sanitation and clean water to impacted communities in Gayo Lues, while floodwaters persist in Aceh Singkil and Subulussalam. Meteorological agencies have issued warnings regarding potential tidal flooding in coastal areas, including the coast of Banten, which is expected to continue through late November. Relief efforts and disaster response teams remain on alert across multiple vulnerable provinces as they manage the ongoing environmental crisis.",
